# Java conventions

- Tabs, constructor injection, no Lombok, no `@Autowired`.
- `service/` is the interface. `service/impl/` is the `@Service` class. Controllers depend on the interface and receive DTOs.
- API bodies are records under `dto/{auth,user,event,order,ticket,common}/`. Entities stay in the persistence layer. Map with `from(...)` on the response record.
- Controllers return `ApiResponse.builder()...response()`. Mutating endpoints set `status` + `message`.
- Domain errors: `ApiException.orNotFound(...)` or `ApiException.conflict(...)`. Never leak stack traces.
- `@Transactional` on purchase, cancel, check-in. Quota changes use `TicketTypeRepository.findByIdForUpdate`.
- JWT subject and `Authentication.getName()` are the user email.
- Password is `@JsonIgnore` on `User`. `Ticket.qr` is `@Transient`. API JSON is DTO records, not entities.
- Secrets (`JWT_SECRET`, `DB_PASSWORD`, `POSTGRES_PASSWORD`, `RESEND_API_KEY`, `RESEND_FROM`) live in env / `.env`, not in `application.properties`.
- Table names: `users`, `orders`, `auth_sessions`. IDs are `GenerationType.IDENTITY`.

## Tests

- Never use the `new` keyword in test code. Build entities with their static factories through `TestData`; use static factories from libraries (`Executors.newFixedThreadPool`, `HttpClient.newHttpClient`, `assertDoesNotThrow`).
- Unit tests: `@ExtendWith(MockitoExtension.class)`, collaborators and request records as `@Mock`, class under test as `@InjectMocks`.
- Integration tests: extend `ApiIntegrationTest` (`@SpringBootTest` + MockMvc, profile `test`). Dependencies are `private final` fields set in the constructor; `junit-platform.properties` enables `spring.test.constructor.autowire.mode=all`, so no `@Autowired`. Send requests through `perform(...)`.
- Database is real Postgres via Testcontainers `jdbc:tc:` URL in `application-test.properties` (Docker must be running). Use unique emails/names per test instead of cleaning tables.
